     We received some good news a few weeks ago: Standard &amp;=20
Poor=92s raised our credit rating to AAA, which is the highest=20
rating it bestows.  Only 15 other U.S. industrial or property-
casualty companies are rated AAA, down from 28 in 1980.

     Corporate bondholders have taken their lumps in the past few=20
years from =93event risk.=94 This term refers to the overnight=20
degradation of credit that accompanies a heavily-leveraged=20
purchase or recapitalization of a business whose financial=20
policies, up to then, had been conservative.  In a world of=20
takeovers inhabited by few owner-managers, most corporations=20
present such a risk.  Berkshire does not.  Charlie and I promise=20
bondholders the same respect we afford shareholders.

